# Agent validation (permanent standard)

One standard for every commit, phase, and PR prep. **Not** a fast iteration
mode — agents never default to broad pre-push, CI-parity, golden, or
whole-package suites before commit or push.

## Dart / Flutter

On each changed path in the commit or uncommitted chunk:

- **`lib/` / `bin/`** — `dart analyze --fatal-infos` on that file only
  (or MCP `analyze_files` with explicit paths).
- **Directly covering tests** — only test files that exercise the changed
  code (`flutter test <path>` or explicit-path `pnpm agent-validate`).

```bash
pnpm agent-validate -- flutter/packages/foo/lib/a.dart flutter/packages/foo/test/a_test.dart
```

`pnpm agent-validate` without paths may inspect uncommitted changes in
some consumer repos — still scoped to the diff, never whole-package.
Always prefer passing explicit paths.

## Non-Dart

Run only analyzers and tests that directly apply to the changed paths.

## During edits

- **ReadLints** on changed files is sufficient between scoped runs.
- Do **not** run MCP `test` on a whole package, `pnpm prepush`,
  `push-gate`, or unscoped `very_good test` / `flutter test` as a
  commit gate.

## Optional full suites (explicit only)

Full package test, `/green-gate`, goldens, and plan `VERIFICATION COMMAND`
runs are for **CI, humans, or explicit user request** — not automatic
agent gates before commit.

## Shell vs MCP (Dart)

| Command | When |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm agent-validate` with explicit paths | Scoped validation before commit |
| `ReadLints` | Between scoped runs on touched files |
| MCP `analyze_files` (scoped paths) | When ReadLints is empty or paths need URI roots |
| MCP `test` (whole package) | Only when user explicitly asks for full package |
| Shell `dart test` / `flutter test` / `very_good test` unscoped | **Never** as a commit gate — use scoped `pnpm agent-validate` |

## MCP bootstrap

`~/.cursor/mcp.json` includes `very-good-cli` when **vgv-ai-flutter-plugin**
is enabled. Scoped validation does not require whole-package MCP `test`.

## Hooks

If hooks block scoped analyze or scoped test commands, report the blocker
and repair hooks — never bypass with `prepush`, whole-package MCP `test`,
or other broad commands.

## MCP `test` exit code 66

Known cwd bug for whole-package MCP `test` — only when the user
explicitly requests that separate work (not a commit gate).
